WEBVTT

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:12.000
This tree is my mother.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.470
As long as I have this 
tree, no one can defeat me.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:24.040
The Ignis will soon vanish, 
along with LINK VRAINS.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:29.230
I promise to fulfill Revolver’s noble goal.

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:31.020
But you'll be erased too!

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:32.750
I know that.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:38.210
Revolver gave me a home.  If 
this is his will, so be it.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:42.000
You’ll sacrifice yourself for Revolver?

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:46.450
A victim of that incident can 
feel something other than hate?

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:51.180
Everyone’s opinions are different.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:01:01.080
A small man like you obsessed with revenge 
can never understand me or Revolver.

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:19.700
I run Across the universe

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:22.870
At the speed of light

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:24.740
Begin Loading

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:28.480
Open the door of dreams

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:32.050
VRAINS spreads

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:35.150
Believe in myself

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:38.690
VRAINS continues

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:44.000
The circuit draws the future

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:48.070
I'll grab it with my own hands  Yeah

00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:49.670
Access!

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:52.370
Start swirling, Data Storm!

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:53.970
I'm now With the Wind

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:56.270
Link with my soul

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:59.040
Speed up, Data Storm!

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:00.780
Now Win the Race

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:03.620
Connected world

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:07.120
No matter when

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:10.490
Nothing is impossible

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:14.630
Strive for hope

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:19.210
And ride the wind!

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:39.480
Your first attack ended 
in a spectacular failure.

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:41.440
What'll you do next?

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:44.670
Multi Sledgehammer’s effect activates!

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:50.320
When another Cyberse Link Monster 
attacks, I place one Hammer Counter.

00:02:50.990 --> 00:02:54.440
I activate Binary Sorceress’s effect!

00:02:54.440 --> 00:03:00.260
Once per turn, by halving my monster's 
ATK until the end of the turn...

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:04.230
...another monster gains that ATK.

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:07.820
I halve Binary Sorceress’s ATK.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:12.080
Binary Blader gains that amount - 800 ATK!

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:18.150
Let's battle!  Binary Blader 
attacks Sunvine Gardna!

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:20.750
Binary Blader’s effect activates!

00:03:20.750 --> 00:03:23.920
It can attack twice during battle!

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:24.720
What?

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:29.680
When this effect activates, your 
monster won't be destroyed in battle.

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:32.090
But you take 2000 damage.

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:34.470
Gardna’s effect activates!

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:39.060
Since it's linked to Sunavalon, 
battle damage is decreased by 800

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:41.840
for each of Sunavalon's Link Markers.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:45.720
So the damage is 1200.

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:48.370
Binary Sorceress’s effect activates!

00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:53.850
When a monster mutually linked with 
her deals you battle damage...

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:56.850
...I regain that amount of LP.

00:03:56.850 --> 00:03:59.720
And Multi Sledge’s effect!

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:02.190
I place one Hammer Conter.

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:04.480
Since I took battle damage...

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:08.820
...I activate the Continuous 
Trap, Sunavalon Glorious Growth!

00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:11.650
I Special Summon a Sunvine Token!

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:19.600
Appear!  The future circuit 
that lights up our path!

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:23.840
Eek!  He’s Link Summoning during our turn?

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:27.570
It's Glorious Growth’s effect.

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:32.020
I’m allowed to Link 
Summon during your turn.

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:36.320
The summoning conditions are 
at least two Plant monsters.

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:43.800
I set Sunvine Token, Gardna and 
Sunavalon Dryas in the Link Markers!

00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:46.910
Link Summon!

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:51.480
Appear, Link 3 Sunavalon Dryanome!

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:56.980
He really Link Summoned.

00:04:58.210 --> 00:05:04.220
Like me, my cards surpass your expectations.

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:07.220
We're in trouble unless you try harder.

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:08.460
I know.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:12.250
Due to Glorious Growth’s additional effect,

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:16.460
I regain LP equal to the damage I just took.

00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:20.170
And you take that same damage!

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:25.200
Your LP are back to its start.

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:27.740
As long as he has Sunavalon...

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:31.210
...even if we damage his LP, 
he’ll just regain them.

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:33.680
It’s the ultimate defense deck.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:39.690
I bet Blue Angel couldn't erase all 
his LP and fell for his tricks.

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:43.560
At this rate, we’ll end 
up the same as Blue Angel!

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:49.080
By the way, Dryanome and 
Dryas can’t be attacked.

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:51.800
You'll attack me directly instead.

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:54.560
He definitely wants us to attack him.

00:05:54.560 --> 00:05:56.030
And I have to.

00:05:56.030 --> 00:05:59.040
Binary Blader attacks you directly!

00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:10.480
Due to Binary Sorceress’s effect, 
Playmaker gains LP equal to the damage - 2600!

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:12.810
6600 LP?

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:14.950
How’s that!

00:06:14.950 --> 00:06:15.830
However…

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:22.520
When I take battle or effect damage, 
Dryanome’s effect activates!

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:24.650
Up to three times during our turns...

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:30.030
...I can Special Summon a Sunvine Link 
Monster next to Sunavalon’s link.

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:32.330
Come, Sunvine Gardna!

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:40.280
And I regain LP equal to the damage I took.

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:44.180
I knew he’d regain LP!

00:06:44.180 --> 00:06:49.840
Then due to Glorious Growth, you take 
damage equal to the amount I regained!

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:54.400
It’s just like before!

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:56.360
Multi Sledge’s effect!

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:58.720
I place one Hammer Counter!

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:01.330
Multi Sledge’s additional effect!

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:06.850
When there’s a monster on your field and 
this card is mutually linked with a Cyberse...

00:07:06.850 --> 00:07:08.600
...it can attack you directly!

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:10.910
That’s pointless.

00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:15.000
Even if you attack me 
directly and shave my LP...

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:19.080
...you know I’ll regain them 
using Dryanome’s effect.

00:07:19.490 --> 00:07:22.090
Multi Sledge has another effect.

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:27.790
When it declares an attack, I remove all 
Hammer Counters to activate its effect!

00:07:29.790 --> 00:07:36.570
It gains 1000 ATK for every removed 
Counter until the end of the turn!

00:07:38.800 --> 00:07:41.100
It powered up!

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:42.410
Attack him directly!

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:47.560
You'll run out of LP before you 
can use Sunavalon’s effect!

00:07:48.290 --> 00:07:50.750
Your plan is to finish him with one strike!

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:52.700
Oh no!

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:58.650
You repeatedly dealt ineffective attacks 
in order to finish me with a single strike?

00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:01.720
What an incredible strategy!

00:08:02.050 --> 00:08:05.480
Our strategy was superior to yours!

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:09.560
But it wasn’t perfect.

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:13.540
Glorious Growth’s effect.

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:17.580
Once per turn, when your 
monster attacks me directly...

00:08:17.580 --> 00:08:20.680
...that attack is negated!

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:29.690
And that monster must attack a Sunvine.

00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:33.760
Gardna’s effect activates!

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:38.130
The damage I take decreases 
from 3400 to 1000!

00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:46.930
No!  He dodged our come-from-behind attack!

00:08:46.930 --> 00:08:50.170
Phew.  I was in real danger.

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:53.980
Due to Binary Sorceress’s 
effect, I regain LP.

00:08:57.120 --> 00:09:02.560
Due to Dryanome’s effect, Sunvine Gardna 
is Special Summoned next to its link.

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:11.600
And I regain LP.

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:14.070
Again?  I’m sick of this!

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:19.770
Then due to Glorious Growth’s 
effect, you take damage.

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:25.980
And Gardna’s effect activates.

00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:30.440
Since it was destroyed, the battle ends.

00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:33.950
This is bad.  The pace is on his side.

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:40.160
Exactly.  This duel is clearly 
heading towards your defeat.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:43.160
I set one card and end my turn.

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:49.400
Binary Sorceress and Multi Sledge’s 
effects end, so their ATK return to normal.

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:56.810
My giant mother tree has no weaknesses.

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:02.310
Boss, don't get too close!  It's dangerous!

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:06.100
But the anonymous viewer's 
coordinates are near here!

00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:08.860
Don’t be scared!  We almost have the scoop!

00:10:08.860 --> 00:10:12.190
Getting a scoop is pointless 
if we get erased!

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:16.440
Even if we’re erased, our 
scoop will live forever.

00:10:16.440 --> 00:10:20.530
That's what a journalist wants!

00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:22.430
Boss, you’re so cool!

00:10:24.410 --> 00:10:25.840
Over there!

00:10:26.190 --> 00:10:28.480
Playmaker is dueling!

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:31.560
All right!  Go!

00:10:32.660 --> 00:10:35.160
Stop stop stop!

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:37.340
It's too dangerous.  Keep your distance.

00:10:37.340 --> 00:10:39.920
That’s the opposite of what you said!

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:46.720
Good.  They arrived at Yusaku’s location.

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:53.040
He's the one who defeated Blue Angel.

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:56.370
We both experienced the Lost Incident.

00:10:56.370 --> 00:10:59.490
But since you're obsessed with revenge

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:03.460
while I'm trying to save the 
world by serving Revolver...

00:11:03.460 --> 00:11:06.490
...this match was decided from the start.

00:11:07.340 --> 00:11:09.470
It hasn’t been decided yet!

00:11:09.470 --> 00:11:15.470
Then I'll begin the countdown 
to your defeat and destruction.

00:11:15.470 --> 00:11:18.460
My turn.  I draw.

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:25.140
I discard one card to activate the 
Continuous Spell, Sunvine Shrine!

00:11:25.540 --> 00:11:29.550
Once per turn, I can Special Summon a Level 4

00:11:29.550 --> 00:11:34.570
or lower Plant Normal 
Monster from the graveyard.

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:37.700
Come, Sunseed Genius Loci!

00:11:37.700 --> 00:11:42.120
Appear!  The future circuit 
that lights up our path!

00:11:42.460 --> 00:11:45.820
The summoning condition is one Plant monster.

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:48.960
I set Genius Loci in the Link Marker!

00:11:49.240 --> 00:11:50.750
Link Summon!

00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:54.440
Appear, Link 1 Sunvine Thrasher!

00:11:56.820 --> 00:11:58.900
Thrasher’s effect activates!

00:11:58.900 --> 00:12:05.980
Since it's linked to Sunavalon, it gains 800 
ATK for each of Sunavalon's Link Markers.

00:12:08.440 --> 00:12:12.970
Let's battle.  Thrasher 
attacks Binary Blader!

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:15.520
This is bad!

00:12:15.520 --> 00:12:17.530
3200 ATK?

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:20.730
Binary Sorceress’s effect activates!

00:12:20.730 --> 00:12:28.200
I halve Multi Sledge’s ATK 
and give it to Binary Blader!

00:12:35.340 --> 00:12:37.790
Thrasher’s effect activates!

00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:44.180
The monster destroyed in battle is Special 
Summoned next to Sunavalon’s link on my field.

00:12:44.180 --> 00:12:45.220
What?

00:12:45.220 --> 00:12:46.780
Binary Blader?

00:12:47.150 --> 00:12:52.020
Blue Angel also let me 
borrow many of her friends.

00:12:57.780 --> 00:12:59.790
He stole his monster!

00:12:59.790 --> 00:13:00.760
This is bad!

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:05.370
Let's battle.  Binary Blader 
attacks Binary Sorceress!

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:12.170
You’re getting pummeled!

00:13:12.170 --> 00:13:14.440
But now he's out of moves.

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:17.900
He can no longer use Dryanome’s effect

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:21.650
to Special Summon monsters next to its link.

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:25.770
If he can't regain LP, I have 
a chance to win next turn!

00:13:26.500 --> 00:13:28.490
I can't believe you noticed that!

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:31.170
That’s why you’re Playmaker!

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:36.130
Someone said the same thing earlier.

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:39.600
I summon Genius Loci for a third time!

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:46.090
Appear!  The future circuit 
that lights up our path!

00:13:46.090 --> 00:13:49.220
The summoning conditions 
are two Plant monsters!

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:54.350
I set Sunvine Gardna and Genius 
Loci in the Link Markers!

00:13:55.050 --> 00:13:56.670
Link Summon!

00:13:56.670 --> 00:14:00.720
Appear, Link 2 Sunavalon Daphne!

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:06.430
A new Sunavalon.

00:14:07.570 --> 00:14:11.940
Sunavalon isn’t just a giant mother tree.

00:14:11.940 --> 00:14:15.710
Daphne expands my link.

00:14:15.710 --> 00:14:19.080
No way!  There's another link!

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:23.690
Sunavalon is a sacred tree 
that stretches its branches.

00:14:23.690 --> 00:14:27.360
He can bring out another Sunvine.

00:14:27.360 --> 00:14:31.150
Yes, Playmaker.  Your chance 
has turned into a pinch.

00:14:31.150 --> 00:14:35.900
I tribute Binary Blader to 
activate Daphne’s effect.

00:14:37.440 --> 00:14:41.430
I return two Gardnas in my 
graveyard to my Extra Deck!

00:14:41.430 --> 00:14:45.040
Now I have two open links.

00:14:46.120 --> 00:14:49.710
I set one card and end my turn.

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:54.380
W-W-What?

00:14:54.380 --> 00:14:58.430
This bridge is about to be destroyed.

00:15:09.330 --> 00:15:12.740
Let’s continue.  It’s your turn.

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:16.500
We're gonna be flipped upside-down!

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:18.100
My turn!  I draw!

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:21.740
I activate the Continuous 
Trap, Sunavalon Force!

00:15:21.740 --> 00:15:27.580
As long as I have this card, your cards’ 
effects can’t be used on Sunavalon.

00:15:27.580 --> 00:15:31.370
Now both attacks and effects 
won’t work against it.

00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:34.940
It’s totally protected!  We gotta 
do something about that tree!

00:15:34.940 --> 00:15:36.450
There are other strategies.

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:38.980
I summon Draconnet!

00:15:40.860 --> 00:15:44.490
What if he summons another Sunvine?

00:15:44.490 --> 00:15:46.170
We have no margin for error!

00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:50.070
When it's summoned, I Special Summon

00:15:50.070 --> 00:15:54.650
a Level 2 or lower Normal Monster 
from my deck in defense position.

00:15:54.650 --> 00:15:56.440
Come, Bitron!

00:15:58.510 --> 00:16:01.580
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:05.720
The summoning condition 
is one Normal Monster!

00:16:06.030 --> 00:16:08.160
I set Bitron!

00:16:08.540 --> 00:16:09.740
Link Summon!

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:13.740
Appear, Link 1 Link Spider!

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:17.660
Link Spider’s effect activates!

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:22.470
Once per turn, I Special Summon a 
Level 4 or lower Normal Monster

00:16:22.470 --> 00:16:25.040
from my hand next to its link.

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:28.640
I Special Summon Digitron from my hand!

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:34.180
Appear again!  The circuit 
that leads to the future!

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:37.220
The summoning conditions 
are two Effect Monsters!

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:40.990
I set Link Spider and Draconnet!

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:43.290
Link Summon!

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:47.190
Appear, Link 2 Underclock Taker!

00:16:47.450 --> 00:16:49.020
Link 2.

00:16:49.230 --> 00:16:50.440
I’m not done!

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:52.900
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:56.640
The summoning conditions are 
at least Cyberse monsters!

00:16:56.640 --> 00:17:00.970
I set Digitron and Link 2 Multi Sledgehammer!

00:17:03.670 --> 00:17:05.010
Link Summon!

00:17:05.010 --> 00:17:09.230
Appear, Link 3 Excode Talker!

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:19.950
500 ATK and can’t be destroyed by effects!

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:22.090
That's pointless.

00:17:22.090 --> 00:17:25.060
My giant mother tree has no weaknesses.

00:17:25.320 --> 00:17:27.530
Excode’s additional effect!

00:17:27.530 --> 00:17:32.140
When it’s Link Summoned, for every 
monster in the Extra Monster Zone...

00:17:32.140 --> 00:17:35.330
...one of your Main Monster 
Zones can’t be used!

00:17:35.330 --> 00:17:36.530
Grasp Zone!

00:17:38.520 --> 00:17:41.970
There are two monsters in 
the Extra Monster Zone!

00:17:45.520 --> 00:17:46.580
What's this?

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:50.250
Underclock Taker’s effect activates!

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:57.990
Once per turn, your monster loses ATK equal 
to the monster next to Underclock's link!

00:17:57.990 --> 00:18:00.360
Next to its link is Excode!

00:18:00.360 --> 00:18:04.330
Thrasher loses 2300 ATK!

00:18:05.290 --> 00:18:10.160
Since you can't attack or affect Sunavalon, 
you’re going after Thrasher-

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:15.940
You can’t use you links right now, so 
Dryanome’s restoration combo can’t be used!

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:17.490
Playmaker!

00:18:18.010 --> 00:18:20.260
We'll succeed this time!

00:18:20.260 --> 00:18:22.320
Oh well.

00:18:22.320 --> 00:18:25.720
I'll have to use my trump card.

00:18:29.890 --> 00:18:30.930
Zaizen?

00:18:31.230 --> 00:18:32.290
Playmaker!

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:34.160
Why is Zaizen there?

00:18:34.490 --> 00:18:39.650
He came to rescue his sister, 
and that's how he ended up.

00:18:39.650 --> 00:18:42.400
So I formed a plan.

00:18:42.990 --> 00:18:48.010
Those thorns contain a computer virus, 
so touching it will infect him.

00:18:48.010 --> 00:18:49.170
What?

00:18:49.170 --> 00:18:50.980
If I get hurt…

00:18:54.920 --> 00:18:59.360
The viral thorns will grow.

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:01.480
Fun, right?

00:19:01.480 --> 00:19:05.720
So feel free to deal me damage.

00:19:05.720 --> 00:19:08.730
That’s cheating!  I hate you!

00:19:08.730 --> 00:19:12.130
Dragging someone who has 
nothing to do with this duel?

00:19:12.130 --> 00:19:14.540
You play very dirty!

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:16.080
"Dragging someone"?

00:19:17.990 --> 00:19:20.900
Did you actually say that?

00:19:20.900 --> 00:19:22.510
Hilarious.

00:19:22.510 --> 00:19:24.610
It’s not funny at all!

00:19:24.900 --> 00:19:31.850
Not counting this duel, do you know 
how many people you dragged into this?

00:19:32.820 --> 00:19:36.290
Why is Blue Angel a casualty?

00:19:37.380 --> 00:19:42.740
It all started because you hid the Ignis.

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:47.040
You dragged him into this too.

00:19:47.730 --> 00:19:50.270
Playmaker!  Don’t worry about me!

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:56.280
Hey!  You don’t need to listen 
to this pompous villain!

00:19:57.630 --> 00:19:59.280
I end my turn.

00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:00.520
What?

00:20:00.520 --> 00:20:02.380
Playmaker...

00:20:04.220 --> 00:20:08.390
Yes.  That's your virtue and your weakness.

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:12.750
I’ve been watching how you battled.

00:20:13.090 --> 00:20:15.590
You can’t be cruel.

00:20:15.590 --> 00:20:20.840
You talk of revenge, but you can’t 
abandon people during a fight.

00:20:21.820 --> 00:20:26.280
Somewhere in your heart, 
there's always justice.

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:32.080
If you don’t hold on to it, you can’t 
bear the weight of your revenge.

00:20:32.430 --> 00:20:34.560
Your spirit is weak.

00:20:34.560 --> 00:20:40.050
In order to save him, you gave 
up your one and only chance.

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:43.120
You’re weak.  Too weak!

00:20:44.030 --> 00:20:50.630
Underclock Taker’s effect ends, so 
Thrasher’s ATK return to normal.

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:54.000
Just when you had a chance…

00:20:58.230 --> 00:21:00.480
The undefeated Playmaker…

00:21:00.480 --> 00:21:06.410
Due to your lame sense of justice, this will 
be your first and last pathetic defeat!

00:21:06.410 --> 00:21:09.410
I'll make sure of that.

00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:12.790
My turn.  I draw!

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:18.760
Let's battle!  Thrasher 
attacks Underclock Taker!

00:21:24.070 --> 00:21:29.100
When your monster is destroyed in battle, 
Sunavalon Force’s effect activates!

00:21:29.840 --> 00:21:37.680
Looking at the monster with the most Link 
Markers, you take 100 damage per Link Marker!

00:21:38.610 --> 00:21:41.790
The most has three Link Markers.

00:21:41.790 --> 00:21:44.410
Therefore, 300 damage.

00:21:52.920 --> 00:21:54.540
The bridge!

00:22:08.850 --> 00:22:15.670
My life is like detestably bad graffiti

00:22:16.060 --> 00:22:22.810
But when you looked at 
me, I felt I wasn't alone

00:22:23.230 --> 00:22:30.040
I'm glad that I'm alive  I truly am

00:22:30.540 --> 00:22:37.390
What I couldn't say before, I can say now

00:22:38.240 --> 00:22:44.630
Within the sadness that I kept holding down

00:22:45.010 --> 00:22:48.780
There were fragments of power

00:22:49.010 --> 00:22:55.960
No one can take away my light to the future

00:22:56.190 --> 00:23:03.300
The chronicles of life only has a few lines

00:23:03.430 --> 00:23:10.480
People I meet, my regrets – they're 
all like ultramarine diamonds to me

00:23:10.730 --> 00:23:17.710
You've always confront loneliness by yourself

00:23:17.840 --> 00:23:24.590
I bet we can now laugh 
together, forever and ever

00:23:25.280 --> 00:23:32.260
Lighting Life with our invisible bond

00:23:36.440 --> 00:23:40.160
When he was young, it was his only place.

00:23:40.160 --> 00:23:44.440
A boring place with a large tree.

00:23:44.440 --> 00:23:49.390
But when he was close to the 
tree, he felt strangely calm.

00:23:49.390 --> 00:23:54.380
Its warmth was the same as a mother's love.

00:23:54.380 --> 00:23:59.120
I only have one chance to 
destroy his perfect Sunavalon.

00:23:59.390 --> 00:24:03.110
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
My Mother Tree

00:24:03.110 --> 00:24:05.110
Into the VRAINS!
